Cold-boot wallpaper retry for TCL G03 AR05 and similar firmware.

On this build, the launcher starts before /sdcard is readable, so the wallpapers
folder enumerates as empty on first launch and Home comes up with no picture
until a manual force-stop of the launcher. The fix below schedules one Activity
recreate() when the symptoms match (wallpaper enabled + rotation > 0 + zero
images found + within 60s of boot). A per-process static flag ensures the retry
runs at most once per boot, so a genuinely empty wallpapers folder does not loop.

Apply from the cleanyourtv checkout root with:
  git apply patches/01-cold-boot-wallpaper-retry.patch
Six lines of logic plus a static field. Costs nothing on normal boots: the
cfg.wallpapers.isEmpty() check skips the block when wallpapers loaded fine.

Reported in https://github.com/Willizxy/tcl-tv-cleanup

diff --git a/launcher/app/src/main/java/com/gathin/tvhome/MainActivity.java b/launcher/app/src/main/java/com/gathin/tvhome/MainActivity.java
index 1796144..1674d07 100644
--- a/launcher/app/src/main/java/com/gathin/tvhome/MainActivity.java
+++ b/launcher/app/src/main/java/com/gathin/tvhome/MainActivity.java
@@ -140,6 +140,9 @@ public class MainActivity extends Activity implements AppAdapter.TileListener {
     private RecyclerView grid;
     private FrameLayout root;
     private WallpaperPlayer wallpaperPlayer;
+    /** Cold-boot wallpaper retry: set once per process after one Activity recreate, so the retry does
+     *  not loop even if the wallpapers folder is genuinely empty. */
+    private static boolean coldBootWallpaperRetryDone = false;
     private GlassView glass;
     private View ambient;
     private TextView heroName;
@@ -434,6 +437,19 @@ public class MainActivity extends Activity implements AppAdapter.TileListener {
         // the theme's background, so launch looks the same.
         getWindow().setBackgroundDrawable(null);
         wallpaperPlayer = new WallpaperPlayer(this, root, cfg);
+        // Cold-boot workaround (TCL G03 AR05 and similar): the launcher can start before /sdcard is
+        // ready and the wallpapers folder enumerates as empty, leaving Home with no picture until a
+        // manual force-stop. If the theme asks for a rotating wallpaper but Config found zero images
+        // within a minute of boot, recreate the Activity once after a short delay. coldBootWallpaperRetryDone
+        // caps this at one retry per process so a genuinely empty wallpapers folder does not loop.
+        if (!coldBootWallpaperRetryDone
+                && SystemClock.elapsedRealtime() < 60_000L
+                && cfg.wallpaperEnabled
+                && cfg.wallpaperRotationMinutes > 0
+                && cfg.wallpapers.isEmpty()) {
+            coldBootWallpaperRetryDone = true;
+            root.postDelayed(this::recreate, 2500L);
+        }
         sky = findViewById(R.id.sky);
         sky.setIntensity(cfg.skyIntensity);
         glass = findViewById(R.id.glass);
